WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.888
The ablations cleanly separate the two biases.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:07.857
On Fashion MNIST, when the nudge is made large,
classic one-sided EP falls apart,

00:00:07.937 --> 00:00:11.825
its error ballooning to thirty-eight point four percent.

00:00:11.905 --> 00:00:15.793
The holomorphic Cauchy-integral estimate with six
points instead stays at fourteen point three percent,

00:00:15.873 --> 00:00:19.762
essentially matching the true derivative at
fourteen point seven percent,

00:00:19.842 --> 00:00:23.730
proof that finite-nudge bias is fully removed.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:27.698
Separately,

00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:31.667
dropping from the exact derivative to a coarse
two-point estimate costs about three points on CIFAR-10,

00:00:31.747 --> 00:00:35.635
quantifying the residual nudge bias.

00:00:35.715 --> 00:00:39.603
And an architecture whose output feeds straight
back to the first layer,

00:00:39.683 --> 00:00:43.572
with no reciprocal connections, benefits just as much,

00:00:43.652 --> 00:00:47.540
confirming the loss targets functional symmetry
rather than weight symmetry.
